hadiths[177]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3966","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik that:The Prophet [SAW] said: ""I have been commanded to fight the idolators until they bear witness to La ilaha illallah (there is none worthy of worship except Allah) and that Muhammad is His slave and Messenger. If they bear witness to La ilaha illallah and that Muhammad is His slave and Messenger"
"3967","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik that :The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""I have been commanded to fight the idolators until they bear witness to La ilaha illallah (there is none worthy of worship except Allah) and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah [SAW]. If they bear witness to La ilaha illallah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah [SAW]"
"3968","Maimun bin Siyah asked Anas bin Malik:""O Abu Hamzah"
"3969","It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:""When the Messenger of Allah [SAW] died"
"3970","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""When the Messenger of Allah [SAW] died and Abu Bakr became the Khalifah after him"
"3971","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'I have been commanded to fight the people until they say La ilaha illallah. If they say it then their blood and their wealth are safe from me"
"3972","Abu Hurairah narrated that :The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""I have been commanded to fight the people until they say La ilaha illallah (there is none worthy of worship but Allah). Whoever says La ilaha illallah"
"3973","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""When the Messenger of Allah [SAW] died"
"3974","Abu Hurairah narrated that :The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""I have been commanded to fight the people until they say La ilaha illallah"
"3975","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""So Abu Bakr decided to fight them"
"3976","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'I have been commanded to fight the people until they say La ilaha illallah. If they say it"
"3977","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'I have been commanded to fight the people until they say La ilaha illallah. If they say it"
"3978","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that :The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""We will fight the people until they say La ilaha illallah. If they say La ilaha illallah then their blood and their wealth become forbidden to us"
"3979","It was narrated that An-Nu'man bin Bashir said:""We were with the Messenger of Allah [SAW] and a man came and whispered to him. He said: 'Kill him.' Then he said: 'Does he bear witness to La ilaha illallah (there is none worthy of worship except Allah)?' He said: 'Yes"
"3980","It was narrated from An-Nu'man bin Salim that:A man said to him: ""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] came to us while we were in a tent inside the Masjid of Al-Al-Madinah"
"3981","It was narrated that An-Nu'man bin Salim said:""I heard Aws say: 'The Messenger of Allah [SAW] came to us when we were in a tent.'"" And he quoted the same Hadith"
"3982","It was narrated that An-Nu'man bin Salim said:""I heard Aws say: 'I came to the Messenger of Allah [SAW] among the delegation of Thaqif and I was with him in a tent. Everyone in the tent had gone to sleep except him and I. A man came and whispered to him"
"3983","It was narrated from An-Nu'man bin Salim that:'Amr bin Aws told him that his father Aws said: ""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'I have been commanded to fight the people until they bear witness to La ilaha illallah (there is none worthy of worship except Allah)"
"3984","It was narrated that Abu Idris said:""I heard Mu'awiyah delivering the Khutbah"
"3985","It was narrated from 'Abdullah that:The Prophet [SAW] said: ""No person is killed wrongfully"
"3986","It was narrated that 'Abdullah bin 'Amr bin Al-'As said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'By the One in Whose Hand is my soul"
"3987","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Amr that:The Prophet [SAW] said: ""The extinction of the whole world is less significant before Allah than killing a Muslim man"
"3988","It was narrated that 'Abdullah bin 'Amr said:""Killing a believer is more grievous before Allah than the extinction of the whole world"
"3989","It was narrated that 'Abdullah bin 'Amr said:""Killing a believer is more grievous before Allah than the extinction of the whole world"
"3990","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin Buraidah that his father said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Killing a believer is more grievous before Allah than the extinction of the whole world"
"3991","It was narrated that 'Abdullah said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'The first thing concerning which a person will be brought to account will be the Salah"
"3992","It was narrated that 'Abdullah said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'The first matter concerning which judgment will be passed among the people will be bloodshed"
"3993","It was narrated from 'Abdullah that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""The first matter concerning which scores will be settled among the people on the Day of Resurrection will be bloodshed"
"3994","It was narrated that 'Abdullah said:""The first matter concerning which scores will be settled among the people on the Day of Resurrection will be bloodshed"
"3995","It was narrated that 'Amr bin Shurahbil said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'The first matter concerning which scores will be settled among the people on the Day of Resurrection will be bloodshed"
"3996","It was narrated that 'Abdullah said:""The first matter concerning which scores will be settled among the people will be bloodshed"
"3997","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud that:The Prophet [SAW] said: ""A man will come"
"3998","It was narrated that Abu 'Imran Al-Jawni said:""Jundab said: 'So and so told me that the Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: The slain will bring his killer on the Day of Resurrection and will say: Ask him why he killed me. He will say: I killed him defending the kingdom of so and so.'"" Jundab said: ""So be careful"
"3999","It was narrated from Salim bin Abi Ja'd that:Ibn 'Abbas was asked about someone who killed a believer deliberately"
"4000","It was narrated that Sa'eed bin Jubair said:""The people of Al-Kufah differed concerning this Verse: ""And whoever kills a believer intentionally."" So I went to Ibn 'Abbas and asked him"
"4001","It was narrated that Sa'eed bin Jubair said:""I said to Ibn 'Abbas: 'Can a person"
"4002","It was narrated that Sa'eed bin Jubair said:""Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Laila told me to ask Ibn 'Abbas about two Verses: 'And whoever kills a believer intentionally"
"4003","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas that :Some people used to kill"
"4004","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas that :Some of the people of Shirk came to Muhammad [SAW] and said: ""What you say and call people to is good"
"4005","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas that:The Prophet [SAW] said: ""The slain will bring his killer on the Day of Resurrection with his forelock and his head in his hand"
"4006","It was narrated that Zaid bin Thabit said:""This Verse - 'And whoever kills a believer intentionally"
"4007","It was narrated from Zaid with regard Allah's saying:""And whoever kills a believer intentionally"
"4008","It was narrated that Mujalid bin 'Awf said:""I heard Kharijah bin Zaid bin Thabit narrate that his father said: (The Verse) 'And whoever kills a believer intentionally"
"4009","Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari narrated that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""Whoever comes worshipping Allah and not associating anything with Him"
"4010","It was narrated that 'Ubaidullah bin Abi Bakr said:""I heard Anas say: 'The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: The major sins are: Associating others with Allah (Shirk)"
"4011","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Amr that:The Prophet [SAW] said: ""The major sins are: Associating others with Allah"
"4012","It was narrated from 'Ubaid bin 'Umair that :His father - who was one of the Companions of the Prophet [SAW] - told him: ""A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
"4013","It was narrated that 'Abdullah said:""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
"4014","It was narrated that 'Abdullah said:""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
"4015","It was narrated that 'Abdullah said:""I asked the Messenger of Allah [SAW]"
"4016","It was narrated that 'Abdullah said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'By the One besides Whom there is no other god"
"4017","It was narrated that 'Amr bin Ghalib said:""Aishah said: 'Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: It is not permissible to shed the blood of a Muslim"
"4018","It was narrated that 'Amr bin Ghalib said:""Aishah said: 'O 'Ammar! Do you not know that it is not permissible to shed the blood of a Muslim except in three cases: a life for a life"
"4019","Abu Umamah bin Sahl and 'Abdullah bin 'Amir bin Rabi'ah said:""We were with 'Uthman when he was under siege and we could hear what was said from Al-Balat. 'Uthman came in one day"
"4020","It was narrated that 'Arfajah bin Shuraih Al-Ashja'I said:""I saw the Prophet [SAW] on the Minbar addressing the people. He said: 'After me there will be many calamities and much evil behavior. Whoever you see splitting away from the Jama'ah or trying to create division among the Ummah of Muhammad [SAW]"
"4021","It was narrated that 'Arfajah bin Shuraih said:""The Prophet [SAW] said: 'After me there will be many calamities and much evil behavior.' He raised his hands (and said): 'Whomever you see trying to create division among the Ummah of Muhammad [SAW] when they are all united"
"4022","It was narrated that 'Arfajah said:""I heard the Messenger of Allah [SAW] say: 'After me there will be many calamities and much evil behavior. Whoever wants to create division among the Ummah (of Muhammad [SAW]) when they are all united"
"4023","It was narrated that Usamah bin Sharik said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Any man who goes out and tries to create division among my Ummah"
"4024","Anas bin Malik narrated that:A group of eighty people from 'Ukl came to the Prophet [SAW]"
"4025","It was narrated from Anas that :Some people from 'Ukl came to the Prophet [SAW] but the climate of Al-Madinah did not suit them. The Prophet [SAW] told them to go to the camels that had been given in Sadaqah and drink some of their milk and urine. They did that"
"4026","It was narrated that Anas said:""Eighty men from 'Ukl came to the Messenger of Allah [SAW]"" and he (the narrator) mentioned a similar report up to the words: ""And he did not have (their wounds) cauterized."" And he said: ""They killed the herdsman"
"4027","It was narrated that Anas said:""A group of men from 'Ukl"
"4028","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik that:Some people from 'Uraynah came to the Messenger of Allah [SAW]"
"4029","It was narrated that Anas said:""Some people from 'Uraynah came to the Messenger of Allah [SAW] and the Messenger of Allah [SAW] said to them: 'Why don't you go out to our camels and stay with them and drink their milk and urine?' So they did that"
"4030","It was narrated that Anas said:""Some people from 'Uraynah came to the Messenger of Allah [SAW]"
"4031","It was narrated that Anas said:""Some people from 'Uraynah became Muslim"
"4032","Anas bin Malik narrated that:Some people or some men from 'Ukl"
"4033","Narrated from 'Abdul-A'la:A similar report was narrated from 'Abdul-A'la"
"4034","It was narrated from Anas that :Some people from 'Uraynah camped in Al-Harrah and came to the Messenger of Allah [SAW]. The climate of Al-Madinah did not suit them"
"4035","It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:""Some Bedouin from 'Uraynah came to the Prophet of Allah [SAW] and accepted Islam"
"4036","It was narrated that Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab said:""Some 'Arab people came to the Messenger of Allah [SAW] and accepted Islam"
"4037","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:""Some people raided the milk camels of the Messenger of Allah [SAW]. He caught them and had their hands and feet cut off and their eyes gouged out"
"4038","It was narrated from 'Aishah:""Some people raided the milk camels of the Messenger of Allah [SAW]. They were brought to the Prophet [SAW]"
"4039","It was narrated from Hisham"
"4040","It was narrated that 'Urwah bin Az-Zubair said:""Some people from 'Uraynah raided the milk camels of the Messenger of Allah [SAW] and drove them off"
"4041","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Umar:From the Messenger of Allah [SAW]: ""The Verse about Al-Muharabah was revealed concerning them"
"4042","It was narrated from Abu Az-Zinad that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] had the (hands and feet) of those who drove off his camels cut off"
"4043","It was narrated that Anas said:""The Prophet [SAW] only had the eyes of those people gouged out"
"4044","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik that:A Jewish man killed an Ansari girl for her jewelry"
"4045","It was narrated from Anas that:A man killed an Ansari girl for her jewelry"
"4046","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said"
"4047","It was narrated from Anas who said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] used to stress charity in his sermons"
"4048","It was narrated from 'Aishah that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""It is not permissible to shed the blood of a Muslim except in three cases: An adulterer who had been married"
"4049","It was narrated that Jarir said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'If a slave runs away"
"4050","Jarir used to narrate from the Prophet [SAW]:""If a slave runs away"
"4051","It was narrated that Jarir bin 'Abdullah said:""If a slave runs away to the land of Shirk"
"4052","It was narrated that Jarir said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'If a slave runs away to the land of Shirk"
"4053","It was narrated from Jarir that:The Prophet [SAW] said: ""If a slave runs away to the land of Shirk"
"4054","It was narrated that Jarir said:""Any slave who runs away to the land of Shirk"
"4055","It was narrated that Jarir said:""Any slave who runs away to the land of Shirk"
"4056","It was narrated that Jarir said:""Any slave who runs away from his masters and joins the enemy"
"4057","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that:'Uthman said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah [SAW] say: 'It is not permissible to shed the blood of a Muslim except in three cases: A man who commits adultery after having married; or one who kills intentionally"
"4058","It was narrated that 'Uthman bin 'Affan said:""I heard the Messenger of Allah [SAW] say: 'It is not permissible to shed the blood of a Muslim except in three cases: A man who commits adultery after having married; or one who kills another person"
"4059","Ibn 'Abbas said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Whoever changes his religion"
"4060","It was narrated from 'Ikrimah:""Some people apostatized after accepting Islam"
"4061","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Whoever changes his religion"
"4062","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Whoever changes his religion"
"4063","It was narrated that Al-Hasan said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Whoever changes his religion"
"4064","It was narrated from Anas that :Ibn 'Abbas said: ""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Whoever changes his religion"
"4065","It was narrated from Anas that :'Ali came to some people of Az-Zutt"
"4066","It was narrated from Abu Burdah bin Abi Musa Al-Ash'ari"
"4067","It was narrated from Mus'ab bin Sa'd that his father said:""On the day of the Conquest of Makkah"
"4068","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:""A man from among the Ansar accepted Islam"
"4069","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said concerning Surat An-Nahl - :""Whoever disbelieved in Allah after his belief"
"4070","Ibn 'Abbas narrated that :There was a blind man during the time of the Messenger of Allah [SAW] who had an Umm Walad by whom he had two sons. She used to slander and defame the Messenger of Allah [SAW] a great deal"
"4071","It was narrated that Abu Barzah Al-Aslami said:""A man spoke harshly to Abu Bakr As-Siddiq"
"4072","It was narrated that Abu Barzah said:""Abu Bakr got infuriated with a man"
"4073","It was narrated that Abu Barzah said:""I passed by Abu Bakr and he was furious with one of his companions. I said: 'O Khalifah of the Messenger of Allah"
"4074","It was narrated that Abu Barzah said:""Abu Bakr became infuriated with a man."" He said: ""If you tell me to"
"4075","It was narrated from Abu Nadrah"
"4076","Abu Nasr narrated from Abu Barzah"
"4077","It was narrated from Yunus bin 'Ubaid"
"4078","It was narrated that Safwan bin 'Assal said:""A Jew said to his companion: 'Let us go to this Prophet.' His companion said to him: 'Do not say Prophet; if he hears you"
"4079","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Whoever ties a know and blows on it"
"4080","It was narrated that Zaid bin Arqam said:""A Jewish man cast a spell on the Prophet [SAW]"
"4081","It was narrated from Qabus bin Mukhariq that his father said:""I heard Sufyan Ath-Thawri narrating this Hadith. He said: 'A man came to the Prophet [SAW] and said: ""What if a man comes to me and wants to take my wealth?"" He said: ""Remind him of Allah."" He said: ""What if he pays no heed?"" He said: ""Seek the help of the Muslims around you against him."" He said: ""What if there are no Muslims around me?"" He said: ""Seek the help of the ruler against him."" He said: ""What if the ruler is far away from me?"" He said: ""Fight to defend your wealth until you either become one of the martyrs of the Hereafter"
"4082","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""A man came to the Messenger of Allah [SAW] and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
"4083","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that:A man came to the Messenger of Allah [SAW] and said: ""O Messenger of Allah"
"4084","It was narrated that 'Abdullah bin 'Amr said:""I heard the Messenger of Allah [SAW] say: 'Whoever fights to protect his wealth and is killed"
"4085","It was narrated that 'Abdullah bin 'Amr said:""I heard the Messenger of Allah [SAW] say: 'Whoever fights to protect his wealth and is killed"
"4086","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Amr bin Al-'As that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""Whoever is killed defending his wealth and is killed unjustly"
"4087","It was narrated that 'Abudllah bin 'Amr said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Whoever is killed defending his wealth"
"4088","It was narrated from Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Talhah that he heard 'Abdullah bin 'Amr narrating:From the Prophet [SAW]"
"4089","It was narrated that 'Abdullah bin 'Amr said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Whoever is killed defending his wealth"
"4090","It was narrated from Sa'eed bin Zaid that:The Prophet [SAW] said: ""Whoever is killed defending his wealth"
"4091","It was narrated from Sa'eed bin Zaid that:The Prophet [SAW] said: ""Whoever is killed defending his wealth"
"4092","It was narrated from Sulaiman bin Buraidah that his father said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Whoever is killed defending his wealth"
"4093","It was narrated that Abu Ja'far said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Whoever is killed defending his wealth and is killed unjustly"
"4094","It was narrated from Sa'eed bin Zaid that:The Prophet [SAW] said: ""Whoever fights to protect his wealth and is killed"
"4095","It was narrated that Sa'eed bin Zaid said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Whoever is killed protecting his wealth"
"4096","It was narrated that Abu Ja'far said:""I was sitting with Suwaid bin Muqarrin"
"4097","It was narrated from Ibn Az-Zubair that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""Whoever unsheathes his sword and starts to strike the people with it"
"4098","Abdur-Razzaq narrated:'Abdur-Razzaq narrated a similar report with the same chain"
"4099","It was narrated that Ibn Az-Zubair said:""Whoever wields a weapon and starts to strike (the people) with it"
"4100","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Umar that :The Prophet [SAW] said: ""Whoever bears weapons against us"
"4101","It was narrated that Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri said:""When 'Ali was in Yemen"
"4102","It was narrated that 'Ali said:""I heard the Messenger of Allah [SAW] say: 'At the end of time there will appear young people with foolish minds. Their faith will not pass through their throats"
"4103","it was narrated that Sharik bin Shihab said:""I used to wish that I could meet a man among the Companions of the Prophet [SAW] and ask him about the Khawarij. Then I met Abu Barzah on the day of 'Id"
"4104","Sa'd bin Abi Waqas told us that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""Fighting a Muslim is Kufr and defaming him is evildoing"
"4105","It was narrated that 'Abdullah said:""Defaming a Muslim is evildoing and fighting him is Kufr."" (Sahih Mawquf)"
"4106","It was narrated from Shu'bah"
"4107","It was narrated that 'Abdullah said:""Defaming a Muslim is evildoing and fighting him is Kufr."" (Sahih Mawquf)"
"4108","It was narrated from 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Abdullah"
"4109","It was narrated from Shu'bah who said:""I said to Hammad: 'I heard Mansur"
"4110","It was narrated from Sufyan bin Zubaid"
"4111","It was narrated that 'Abdullah said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Defaming a Muslim is evildoing and fighting him is Kufr"
"4112","It was narrated that Abu Wa'il said:""'Abdullah said: 'Defaming a Muslim is evildoing and fighting him is Kufr"
"4113","It was narrated that 'Abdullah said:""Fighting a believer is Kufr and defaming him is evildoing"
"4114","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Whoever parts from obedience"
"4115","It was narrated that Jundab bin 'Abdullah said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Whoever fights for a cause that is not clear"
"4116","It was narrated that Abu Bakrah said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'If a Muslim points a weapon at his fellow Muslim"
"4117","It was narrated that Abu Bakrah said:""If two Muslim men bear weapons against each other"
"4118","It was narrated from Abu Musa that:The Prophet [SAW] said: ""If two Muslims confront each other with swords"
"4119","It was narrated from Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari that:The Prophet [SAW] said: ""If two Muslims confront each other with swords and one of them kills the other"
"4120","It was narrated from Abu Bakrah that :The Prophet [SAW] said: ""If two Muslims confront each other with swords"
"4121","It was narrated that Abu Bakrah said:""The Messenger [SAW] said: 'If two Muslims meet (and fight) with their swords and one of them kills the other"
"4122","It was narrated that Abu Bakrah said:""I heard the Messenger of Allah [SAW] say: 'If two Muslims confront each other with their swords and one of them kills the other"
"4123","It was narrated that Abu Bakrah said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'If two Muslims fight with swords"
"4124","It was narrated from Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari that :The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""If two Muslims confront each other with swords and one of them kills the other"
"4125","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that :The Prophet [SAW] said: ""Do not revert to disbelievers after I am gone"
"4126","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Do not revert to disbelievers after I am gone"
"4127","It was narrated that 'Abdullah said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Do not revert to disbelievers after I am gone"
"4128","It was narrated that Masruq said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'I do not want to see you after I am gone reverting to disbelievers"
"4129","It was narrated from Masruq that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""Do not revert to disbelievers after I am gone."" It is Mursal"
"4130","It was narrated from Abu Bakrah that:The Prophet [SAW] said: ""Do not revert to misguidance after I am gone"
"4131","It was narrated from Jarir that :During the Farewell Pilgrimage"
"4132","It was narrated that Jarir bin 'Abdullah said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said to me: 'Ask the people to be quiet and listen.' Then he said: 'I do not want to see you after I am gone reverting to disbelievers"
"4133","It was narrated from Yazid bin Hurmuz that:when Najdah Al-Haruriyyah rebelled during the Fitnah of Ibn Zubayr"
"4134","It was narrated that Yazid bin Hurmuz said:""Najdah wrote to Ibn 'Abbas and asked him about the share of the relatives (of the Messenger of Allah)"
"4135","It was narrated that Al-Awza'i said:""Umar bin 'Abdul-'Aziz wrote a letter to 'Umar bin Al-Walid in which he said: 'The share that your father gave to you was the entire Khumus"
"4136","Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab narrated that Jubair bin Mut'im told him:""He and 'Uthman bin 'Affan came to the Messenger of Allah to speak to him about what he had distributed of the Khumus of Hunain to Banu Hashim and Banu Al-Muttalib bin 'Abd Manaf. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
"4137","It was narrated that Jubair bin Mut'im said:""When the Messenger of Allah distributed the share for his relatives to Banu Hashim and BanuA-Muttalib"
"4138","It was narrated that 'Ubadah bin Al-Samit said:""On the day of Hunain the Messenger of Allah took a hair from the side of a camel and said: 'O you people"
"4139","It was narrated from 'Amr bin Shu'aib"
"4140","It was narrated that 'Umar said:""The wealth of Banu An-Nadir was among the Fay' that Allah bestowed upon His Messenger"
"4141","It was narrated from 'Aishah that:Fatimah sent word to Abu Bakr asking for her inheritance from the Prophet"
"4142","It was narrated that 'Ata' said concerning the saying of Allah"